welcome to another technology tuesday  today i'm answering a question for one  of my youtube viewers love you guys  crap stuff who wrote in to say evan  carmichael thanks sir for this amazing  video could you possibly make a video  for those who want to hire  on odesk something like how to hire an  employee on odesk well crap stuff this  is a great question and  i love odess okay i have i have a man  crush on odesk i found such great people  to work with me on exciting projects to  do an amazing job and it's all remote  right nobody's actually sitting here in  your office doing stuff they're all  doing it on their own time when they  want but delivering i've recommended  odesk to a lot of different  entrepreneurs and people have had a hard  time finding the right people and they  wonder how how i'm so lucky compared to  them i have a different hiring process  okay i have a really different hiring  process and not just on oh this is what  i do bringing somebody on locally too i  think the regular hiring systems are  broken and somebody can look really good  on paper right you beef up your resume  some people can do really well in an  interview and they they freeze through  all the interviews but  they don't end up being a great worker  right he end up having to fire them  after three months and and i hate going  through that process  what's more important to me is i want  somebody who loves what we're all about  and is a worker and if you don't have  the answer you'll go and find the answer  that's what i think we need in  entrepreneurial businesses and i've  developed a system for how to find that  on odesk so i'm going to share it with  you and hopefully you can apply it and  be one of the lucky ones who get results  with odesk  so number one is have a skilled testing  question  whenever i post an ad on on odessa and  posting a job posting i always have  usually one big long ugly description  right i don't make it easy for somebody  to read through my job posting a lot of  the reason why is i'm not always a super  detail oriented person but i need my  teammates to be right i need people to  compliment that weakness in me and be  really  detail  oriented so i need them to read this big  job posting big ugly paragraph right and  in the middle  i have a skill testing question and it's  usually something really easy like how  many twitter followers do i have how  many youtube subscribers do i have some  were just buried it's totally random and  it's in the middle of this big chunky  paragraph this question and then people  have to answer that and i say answer  this question in the first line of your  application because what's going to  happen with odesk or anywhere else  people see a job and they apply right  they send their standard resume they  change the name on the cover letter most  of the time and send it to you what  takes them  two minutes of work takes you real time  to screen  right you have to screen all these  resumes you have to screen all these  cover letters and they're chewing up  your time and i hate having my time  chewed up so what i do is  i look for that first sentence  if you haven't told me how many twitter  followers i have you haven't told me how  many youtube subscribers or whatever my  skill testing question is you haven't  put that in your first sentence i'm not  reading your application i don't care  how good you are i don't care about your  background your credentials i don't care  about your references i don't care about  any of that because you're wasting my  time because you did not read my  paragraph  and the people who write in to say  what's your twitter account so i can  answer the question properly it blows my  mind if you can't go and type evan  carmichael twitter and find me  then i don't want to hire you either  so right away i cut out around 80  percent of the people who apply to the  job 80  imagine if i had spent you know if you  get if you get 100 applications and 80  of them are junk and you have to spend  five minutes on each one of those going  through how much time do you lose on  that it blows my mind so if you gotta  answer my question number one have your  skill test in question  number two is hire for a small job so if  you answered my question typically what  i'll then do is i again i don't care  about your previous work on odesk i  don't care if you're brand new i don't  care if you have 2000 hours on it  doesn't matter to me if you answered my  question then i'm going to hire you for  a small sample project and what i  usually do is set a project i set a  limit of five hours and i pay you for it  say hey i'm going to hire you to do this  project and it's a small thing that  relates somehow to what they're going to  be doing right so when i hired christina  who does my video editing i hired her  and i hired a bunch of people and i  hired them for five hours and said hey  here's one video  do what you can with it make it awesome  i give them five hours and what it does  is allow you to test to see  are people doing a good job or not so  first of all it lets me see  are they milking me for the full five  hours or not i actually try to find  something where i think it's going to be  less than five hours maybe it'll take  them three hours to do and so are they  gonna milk me for the full five hours  and say oh yeah i work five hours on  this so they can get the money grab  because i don't want that person working  for me and i just saved a whole bunch of  time figuring that out and i can  eliminate them right away or did they do  it ahead of time right if i say i need  it by done by saturday and here's five  hours to do it do they go all the way to  saturday and take five hours or do they  get it done by thursday and do it in two  hours right that's the hustle that you  want  and then you can look at the quality of  the work  is it good right do they blow you away  the reason why i hired christina is  because she did more than what i asked  her to do  most of the people who submitted it they  just did what i asked him to do they  took they took by intro they put it on  there they put the enter the end  whatever i asked them to do they did it  but they didn't go beyond  where christina said hey here's some  other things you can do with it and  created a new video and i loved it said  her i gotta hire her so always start by  hiring on a small job  and expanding from there number three is  keep the top performers so you'll find  that from that trial job a couple people  will send out it may only be one person  but it may be two or three people i hire  those people if it's one or three  on  a more full-time basis right i hire them  on an ongoing basis and i see who excels  because i believe that you get  a feel for working with somebody pretty  quickly and you can see are they really  working hard are they really pouring  their energy into this are they giving  all of themselves to this are they just  kind of floating by taking a paycheck  right i don't want to be  the guy  on odesk who has to look at your screens  and has to track your keystrokes right  odess gives you that feature you could  you could see everybody's screenshot i  don't want to micromanage people on  odesk or  somebody who is in my office i don't  want to have to manage those people i  want them to be motivated i want them to  work hard i want them to be passionate  what they're doing and so i find those  people  who want to do it and don't waste my  time on everybody else so remember  number one have a skill testing question  number two hire for a small job number  three keep the top performers and  believe  thank you for the great question if you  want to see more videos like this you  can subscribe to my channel and i will  see you soon

